1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Luke 15

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,240
And when he comes home, he calls together his friends and his neighbors, saying to them,

3
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:38,320
Rejoice with me, for I have found my sheep that was lost.

4
00:00:39,320 --> 00:00:44,400
Just so I tell you, there will be more joy in heaven over one sinner who repents

5
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:48,600
than over ninety-nine righteous persons who need no repentance.

6
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:54,220
Or what woman, having ten silver coins, if she loses one coin,

7
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:58,700
does not light a lamp and sweep the house and seek diligently until she finds it?

8
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:03,080
And when she has found it, she calls together her friends and neighbors, saying,

9
00:01:03,460 --> 00:01:06,940
Rejoice with me, for I have found the coin that I had lost.

10
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:14,720
Just so I tell you, there is joy before the angels of God over one sinner who repents.

11
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:16,360
And he said,

12
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:21,240
There was a man who had two sons, and the younger of them said to his father,

13
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:25,040
Father, give me the share of property that is coming to me.

14
00:01:25,420 --> 00:01:27,660
And he divided his property between them.

15
00:01:28,060 --> 00:01:28,660
Not many.

16
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:33,760
Not many days later, the younger son gathered all he had and took a journey into a far country,

17
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:37,340
and there he squandered his property in reckless living.

18
00:01:38,020 --> 00:01:42,040
And when he had spent everything, a severe famine arose in that country,

19
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:43,960
and he began to be in need.

20
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:48,040
So he went and hired himself out to one of the citizens of that country,

21
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:51,400
who sent him into his fields to feed pigs.

22
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:55,540
And he was longing to be fed with the pods that the pigs ate,

23
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:57,640
and no one gave him anything.

24
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:01,100
But when he came to himself, he said,

25
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:05,600
How many of my father's hired servants have more than enough bread?

26
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:07,780
But I perish here with hunger.

27
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:12,460
I will arise and go to my father, and I will say to him,

28
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:16,380
Father, I have sinned against heaven and before you.

29
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:19,200
I am no longer worthy to be called your son.

30
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:22,140
Treat me as one of your hired servants.

31
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:25,720
And he arose and came to his father.

32
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:28,360
But while he was still a long way off,

33
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:31,180
his father saw him and felt compassion,

34
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:34,180
and ran and embraced him and kissed him.

35
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:36,100
And the son said to him,

36
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:39,800
Father, I have sinned against heaven and before you.

37
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:42,480
I am no longer worthy to be called your son.

38
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:44,740
But the father said to his servants,

39
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:48,060
Bring quickly the best robe and put it on him,

40
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:51,440
and put a ring on his hand and shoes on his feet,

41
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:53,940
and bring the fattened calf and kill it,

42
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:55,960
and let us eat and celebrate.

43
00:02:56,580 --> 00:02:58,500
For this my son was dead,

44
00:02:58,700 --> 00:02:59,880
and is alive again.

45
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:01,980
He was lost and is found.

46
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:04,480
And they began to celebrate.

47
00:03:05,720 --> 00:03:07,900
Now his older son was in the field,

48
00:03:08,380 --> 00:03:10,800
and as he came and drew near to the house,

49
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:12,860
he heard music and dancing.

50
00:03:13,340 --> 00:03:16,560
And he called one of the servants and asked what these things meant.

51
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:18,040
And he said to him,

52
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:19,720
Your brother has come,

53
00:03:19,940 --> 00:03:21,860
and your father has killed the fattened calf

54
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:24,580
because he has received him back safe and sound.

55
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:28,220
But he was angry and refused to go in.

56
00:03:28,700 --> 00:03:31,000
His father came out and entreated him.

57
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:32,720
But he answered his father,

58
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:36,680
Look, these many years I have served you,

59
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:39,080
and I never disobeyed your command.

60
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:41,620
Yet you never gave me a young goat

61
00:03:41,620 --> 00:03:43,740
that I might celebrate with my friends.

62
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:46,600
But when this son of yours came,

63
00:03:46,860 --> 00:03:49,560
who has devoured your property with prostitutes,

64
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:52,240
you killed the fattened calf for him.

65
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:54,560
And he said to him,

66
00:03:55,260 --> 00:03:58,040
Son, you were always with me,

67
00:03:58,040 --> 00:04:00,320
and all that is mine is yours.

68
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:03,780
It was fitting to celebrate and be glad,

69
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:07,680
for this your brother was dead and is alive.

70
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:11,380
He was lost and is found.

